pmc:ChaosMagicHypertrophiedSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One self made to hypertrophy and dominate the others"@en, "Ein Selbst, das wuchert und die anderen beherrscht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hypertrophy of one of one's selves to dominate the others, for which monotheism is said to have a certain use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 20; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicParadigmShiftingYieldsHypertrophiedSelf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Monotheism, taken up as a paradigm, lets one self hypertrophy and dominate"@en, "Der Monotheismus, als Paradigma ergriffen, lässt ein Selbst wuchern und herrschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even monotheism is said to have a certain use for those who want just one of their selves to hypertrophy and dominate the others."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicParadigmShifting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicHypertrophiedSelf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 20; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicUnawareParadigmChangeCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Changing paradigms has value only so long as one realizes one is doing so"@en, "Der Paradigmenwechsel hat nur Wert, solange man weiß, dass man ihn vollzieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The value of changing paradigms as readily as one's clothing holds only so long as one realizes that one is doing so; the Golden Dawn, attempting to be animist, spiritist, pagan and monotheist all at once, is given as the ultimate in syncretic metaphysical confusion."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning of the text against a misreading of its own recommendation: the change of paradigm taken without knowing it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:ChaosMagicParadigmShifting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 20; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAnimistParadigmBeforeSorcery a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "For actual magic the spiritist or, preferably, the animist paradigm is required"@en, "Für tatsächliche Magie ist das spiritistische oder besser das animistische Paradigma erforderlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "For actual magic, by which the author means practical sorcery and parapsychology, the spiritist or, preferably, the animist paradigm is said to be required."@en ;
    skos:note "The sentence says required but states no consequence of going without; entered at prescribed order, the grade the shape admits without a cited consequence. The dependent step is the enchantment of the fifth principle, the practical sorcery the sentence names."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicEnchantmentKaos ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:ChaosMagicMana ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 21; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicEther a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ether: information emitted by matter, instantly available everywhere and shaping other matter"@en, "Äther: von Materie ausgesandte Information, überall sofort verfügbar und andere Materie formend"@de ;
    skos:definition "To explain CMT a concept dignified with the old name ether is introduced. It is no more possible to say what ether is than what matter and energy are, only what it does: it acts as though it were a form of information emitted by matter, instantaneously available everywhere, with some power to shape the behavior of other matter, broadly analogous to morphogenetic fields or non-local effects in physics. Ether is a purely descriptive hypothesis, as energy is in physics. CMT is presently a qualitative description, though its practical formulae for simple magics are quantitative; it is potentially quantifiable, and its quantification could represent the unification of magic and science. In the Aeonics chapter ether is described in materialist terms as information which structures matter and which all matter emits and receives, in transcendental terms as a life force present in all things, carrying knowledge about events and the ability to influence similar or sympathetic ones."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 21; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 22; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 2 Aeonics, p. 55; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAbsoluteRealityCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Magicians and scientists should never attribute absolute reality to anything"@en, "Magier und Wissenschaftler sollen nie irgendetwas absolute Wirklichkeit zuschreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ether is a purely descriptive hypothesis: within CMT reality can be described as though it had the properties attributed to ether, as physics describes the universe as having the properties of energy, and neither concept should be regarded as other than a convenient description of experiences and observations. Magicians and scientists should never attribute absolute reality to anything."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning against reading the work's own central term as a substance."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicEther ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 21; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicFivePrinciplesOfCMT a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The five principles of CMT: ether emitted, non-local, shaping like matter, self-coupling, coupling with mind"@en, "Die fünf Grundsätze der CMT: Äther ausgesandt, nichtlokal, Gleiches formend, mit sich koppelnd, mit dem Geist koppelnd"@de ;
    skos:definition "First, all matter emits ether, which carries or consists of information about the matter that emitted it. Second, ether is non-local in space, instantaneously available everywhere. Third, ether has a shaping effect on matter having affinity or similarity with the matter that emitted it, making the behavior of the two more similar; ether is detectable only by this effect, and the coupling gives rise to the physical laws and constants, which arise on a purely chaotic and arbitrary basis and become reliable through repetition, any novel event remaining chaotic though pattern-forming. Fourth, ether couples with itself into patterns corresponding to the possible pasts and futures of any moment, which do not determine the future, since their coupling with matter is probabilistic; initial conditions of an indeterminate event cannot be recovered, and history is called as indeterminate as the future. Fifth, mental events, being material structures, can emit and couple with ether. The five are called the minimum hypothesis for both the ubiquity of physical laws and their occasional violation by chaotic and magical events; they imply a realistic limitation on the power and variety of esoteric effects while confirming that the universe itself is a magical phenomenon. The third presumes that like affects like: only between phenomena or mental events of considerable similarity can a magical link operate."@en ;
    skos:note "The realistic limitation on esoteric effects is stated here without figures; the equations of magic later give it numbers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 22; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 23; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 23; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPastAndFutureCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The trap of supposing that the physical past and future have real existence"@en, "Die Falle, der physischen Vergangenheit und Zukunft wirkliche Existenz zuzuschreiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "One should not fall into the trap, created by memory and expectation, of supposing that the physical past and future have any real existence: only the present moment exists, each with its own unique pattern of past and future. Common sense creates an illusory certainty about the causes of events by imputing reverse causal connections, whereas any and all initial conditions that might have led to the observed result must be admitted. Past and future exist only as memory and expectation, both called mere wishful thinking."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicFivePrinciplesOfCMT ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 23; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Shadow Time, p. 35; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicEnchantmentKaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchantment: a thought or visualization couples with a phenomenon and raises the probability of an event"@en, "Verzauberung: ein Gedanke oder eine Vorstellung koppelt mit einer Erscheinung und erhöht die Wahrscheinlichkeit eines Ereignisses"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under the right conditions a thought or visualization of some phenomenon can create an etheric pattern which couples with that phenomenon to modify its behavior. The fourth principle describes enchantment: etheric patterns forming a spellcasting which sets a form for the manifestation of some event enhance the probability of that event occurring. Most magicians are comfortable with the idea that enchantments can be cast to force, or at least nudge, the hand of chance as far as the future is concerned."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 23; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Retroactive Enchantment, p. 39; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicSpellcasting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Spellcasting: forming an etheric pattern that sets a form for the manifestation of an event"@en, "Zauberwirken: ein ätherisches Muster bilden, das der Manifestation eines Ereignisses eine Form vorgibt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A thought or visualization of a phenomenon creates an etheric pattern which couples with the phenomenon; etheric patterns forming a spellcasting set a form for the manifestation of some event. The same act aimed at preventing an event lowers its probability, and an act of magic may alter the past shadow time of a moment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicSpellcastingYieldsEnchantment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "A spellcasting that sets a form for an event enhances its probability"@en, "Ein Zauber, der einem Ereignis eine Form vorgibt, erhöht seine Wahrscheinlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Etheric patterns forming a spellcasting which sets a form for the manifestation of some event will enhance the probability of that event occurring."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicSpellcasting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicEnchantmentKaos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicDivinationKaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divination: the ether of a phenomenon modifies the mental image of it"@en, "Divination: der Äther einer Erscheinung verändert das geistige Bild von ihr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conversely to enchantment, the ether from some phenomenon can couple with a mental image of that phenomenon and modify it to provide divinatory information. At any moment it may be possible to divine the etheric pattern of the future of that moment and pick the most probable future. CMT allows divination for events hidden in the past or in the future, the magician looking only through shadow time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Retroactive Enchantment, p. 38; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicDivinationProbabilityCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Divination yields only the most probable pasts and futures of the moment at which it is made"@en, "Divination liefert nur die wahrscheinlichsten Vergangenheiten und Zukünfte des Augenblicks, in dem sie geschieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth principle sets a probabilistic limit on divination: the most probable future picked is only a probability, not a certainty, and a divination can only yield information about the future of the moment at which it is performed, since a subsequent moment may have a different future through indeterminacy. Information from parallel universes of low probability and from great imaginary temporal distance is more difficult to detect. Any information found about hidden past or future events represents at best the highest probability events that were likely to have occurred or might occur."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a divined future that does not come is accounted for beforehand by indeterminacy and by the moment of the divination, which puts the failure elsewhere than on the diviner. The outcome is observable; the work sets no count or deadline."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicDivinationKaos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Shadow Time, p. 36; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Retroactive Enchantment, p. 38; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTelepathyKaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telepathy, by the same mechanism that keeps the speed of light constant"@en, "Telepathie, durch denselben Mechanismus, der die Lichtgeschwindigkeit konstant hält"@de ;
    skos:definition "Telepathy occurs because of the same mechanism which keeps the speed of light at a particular constant value; telepathic coupling is less reliable only because there are more differences between two mental events than between any two photon quanta."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 24; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicEnchantLongDivineShort a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Enchant long and divine short"@en, "Lange im Voraus verzaubern, kurz voraus wahrsagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Where possible one should enchant long and divine short: enchantments are cast well in advance, divinations made for the near rather than the far future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicEnchantLongYieldsEnchantment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Enchantments cast well in advance have a greater chance to shift probability"@en, "Lange im Voraus gewirkte Verzauberungen haben größere Aussicht, die Wahrscheinlichkeit zu verschieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Enchantments cast well in advance have a greater chance to modify sequences of probability in one's favor."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicEnchantLongDivineShort ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicEnchantmentKaos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicDivineShortYieldsDivination a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Divinations for the near future give better results"@en, "Divinationen für die nahe Zukunft geben bessere Ergebnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divinations give better results if performed for the near rather than the far future, whose manifestation is more subject to indeterminate chaotic occurrences."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicEnchantLongDivineShort ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicDivinationKaos ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicSpiritsAsEthericPatterns a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spirits as the etheric patterns of phenomena, and gods as created by humanity"@en, "Geister als die ätherischen Muster der Erscheinungen, und Götter als von der Menschheit geschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The etheric pattern associated with any phenomenon can be regarded as its spirit, but it should not be credited with knowledge or powers beyond those of the phenomenon itself. When interacting with the so-called archetypal god and demon forms, the magician is simply establishing a resonance with expressions of ideas and feelings always being projected somewhere in the world, hoping that such resonance will amplify such effects within. Humanity creates gods, not vice versa, but once created they can have profound effects so long as they continue to be worshipped by deed and memory."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAnimalSpiritsCautela a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "An animal spirit that pontificates beyond its ecological speciality is one's own subconscious"@en, "Ein Tiergeist, der über sein ökologisches Fach hinaus doziert, ist das eigene Unbewusste"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spirit should not be credited with knowledge or powers beyond those of its phenomenon; if animal spirits begin to pontificate upon matters outside of their ecological specialities, one should look to the creativity of one's own subconscious for explanation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an observable mark, a spirit speaking beyond its ecological speciality, by which a contact is to be recognised as the operator's own subconscious and not the spirit. The failure is put on the operator."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:ChaosMagicSpiritsAsEthericPatterns ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicGodformResonance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Resonance with archetypal god and demon forms"@en, "Resonanz mit archetypischen Gott- und Dämonenformen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In interacting with the so-called archetypal god and demon forms the magician establishes a resonance with expressions of ideas and feelings which are always being projected somewhere in the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAmplifiedEffectsWithin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The ideas and feelings of a god or demon form amplified within the magician"@en, "Die Ideen und Gefühle einer Gott- oder Dämonenform im Magier verstärkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The amplification within the magician of the ideas and feelings that a god or demon form expresses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicGodformResonanceYieldsAmplifiedEffects a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Resonance with a god or demon form is hoped to amplify its effects within"@en, "Resonanz mit einer Gott- oder Dämonenform soll ihre Wirkungen innen verstärken"@de ;
    skos:definition "The magician establishing resonance with a god or demon form hopes that such resonance will amplify such effects within."@en ;
    skos:note "The work says the magician hopes for it; the claim is entered at that strength."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicGodformResonance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicAmplifiedEffectsWithin ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 25; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicWorshipByDeedAndMemory a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Worship of a god by deed and memory"@en, "Verehrung eines Gottes durch Tat und Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A god created by humanity continues to be worshipped by deed and memory."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 26; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicWorshipBeforeGodEffects a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A created god has effects only so long as it continues to be worshipped"@en, "Ein geschaffener Gott wirkt nur, solange er weiter verehrt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once created by humanity, gods can have profound effects so long as they continue to be worshipped by deed and memory."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:ChaosMagicGodCreation ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:ChaosMagicWorshipByDeedAndMemory ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The created god's profound effects last only so long as it continues to be worshipped by deed and memory." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 26; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicPsychicAnatomy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The psychic anatomy: the ether of the organs (Chi), the soul of memory, and Kia"@en, "Die psychische Anatomie: der Äther der Organe (Chi), die Seele des Gedächtnisses und Kia"@de ;
    skos:definition "The human psychic anatomy consists of the ethers of various levels of organic organization. The ether of the bodily organs, particularly the nervous system, is known in oriental esotericism as Chi or Ki, which various occult martial arts and medicine try to influence, and visualization has begun to find a place in occidental treatment of disease. The etheric patterns of memory and mental activity constitute what used to be called the soul, which cannot be expected to survive bodily decay unless its patterns are replicated in other living minds; reincarnation is thus an act of communication unlikely to be more effective than reproduction or writing a book. Spiritualist seance-effects, at their infrequent best, argue for little more than minor parapsychological abilities, including some telepathic access to the client's memories by the medium. The third part is the Kia. Ether is not superior to matter; matter and ether co-evolve, and the old spirit/matter duality disappears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 26; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 27; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicHealingVisualization a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Occult martial arts, medicine and visualization acting on Chi"@en, "Okkulte Kampfkünste, Medizin und Visualisierung, die auf das Chi wirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Various forms of occult martial arts and medicine operate by trying to influence the ether of the bodily organs and nervous system, Chi or Ki; in occidental medicine visualization has begun to find its place in the treatment of disease."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 26; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

