pmp:ChaosMagicTalismanChargingKaos a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Charging a talisman so that the spell is projected again whenever its charger notices it"@en, "Einen Talisman laden, damit der Zauber erneut ausgesandt wird, sooft sein Lader ihn bemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The purpose of a so-called charged or consecrated talisman is to cause a subsequent projection of the spell it was charged with whenever the person who charged it notices or visualizes it. In no sense does the spell reside within the material basis of the talisman, and the object must be regarded as quite useless to any other person in whom the spell had not been planted."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the talisman is stated to be useless in the hands of anyone in whom the spell was not planted. The failure is put on the bearer, not on the object, and is observable in principle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 28; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicSpellProjection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The renewed projection of a spell each time its talisman is noticed"@en, "Die erneute Aussendung eines Zaubers, sooft sein Talisman bemerkt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "A spell projected again, subsequently and repeatedly, whenever the person who charged its talisman notices or visualizes it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 28; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicTalismanChargingYieldsSpellProjection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "A charged talisman projects its spell whenever its charger notices or visualizes it"@en, "Ein geladener Talisman sendet seinen Zauber aus, sooft sein Lader ihn bemerkt oder vorstellt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A charged talisman causes a subsequent projection of the spell it was charged with whenever the person who charged it notices or visualizes it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:ChaosMagicTalismanChargingKaos ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:ChaosMagicSpellProjection ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
