pmc:ChaosMagicGhostsOfTheDead a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ghosts of the dead as prescience, with wakefulness blinding us to our dreaming"@en, "Geister der Toten als Vorauswissen, wobei das Wachsein uns für unser Träumen blind macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "CMT suggests a new interpretation of ghosts of the dead: in virtually all sightings the witnesses either already possessed an image of the deceased or received confirmation of a perceived image soon after, implying the exercise of prescience. Most ancients would have called meeting a deceased person in a dream or awake seeing a ghost; today most people distinguish the two, but as sunlight obscures the stars by day, so wakefulness blinds us to the fact that we are still dreaming."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 28; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page", "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 29; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmp:ChaosMagicArtificialGhostCreation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating artificial ghosts of persons who never existed"@en, "Künstliche Geister von Personen erschaffen, die nie gelebt haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is called a simple, though laborious, procedure to create artificial ghosts of persons who never existed."@en ;
    skos:note "The procedure is named and not described in this part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
